WEBVTT

00:04:28.292 --> 00:04:30.133
So now I've invented this machine

00:04:30.157 --> 00:04:33.077
to let us explore the microscopic world.

00:04:33.101 --> 00:04:35.061
It's not virtual, it's real.

00:04:35.085 --> 00:04:36.752
Just really, really tiny.

00:04:37.203 --> 00:04:40.156
It's based on the microscope
that got Simone's attention.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.585
So, here's how it works.

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:44.370
I have an image sensor

00:04:44.394 --> 00:04:47.164
like the kind in your cell phone,
behind the lens.

00:04:47.188 --> 00:04:49.656
And then I have a little tray
of plankton water

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.428
like you might find from a river

00:04:51.452 --> 00:04:53.887
or my fish tank, which I never
change the water on.

00:04:53.911 --> 00:04:55.101
(Laughter)

00:04:55.125 --> 00:04:56.300
Because I love plankton.

00:04:56.324 --> 00:04:59.848
(Laughter)

00:04:59.872 --> 00:05:02.998
And underneath I have a light, an LED,